<!--
  ============================================================================
  Only needed if the glyph fails to appear on std::vector<gp_Pnt> specifically.
  Paste these blocks inside the <AutoVisualizer> element of FCCore.natvis.
  ============================================================================

  WHY THIS MIGHT BE NEEDED

  natvis.xsd states the precedence order plainly:

     "regardless of priority, natvis files that are part of a loaded project
      will always take precedence over files in the user natvis directory,
      which will, in turn, take precedence over files in the system-wide
      natvis directory."

  FCCore.natvis is part of a loaded project. PlotBridge.natvis lives in the user
  directory. FCCore.natvis already declares:

      <Type Name="std::vector&lt;gp_Pnt,*&gt;" Inheritable="false">
        ... AlternativeType for gp_Pnt2d, gp_Vec, gp_Vec2d, gp_Dir, gp_Dir2d

  so for those six element types the project entry wins the type match. Whether
  that also suppresses a <UIVisualizer> declared in the losing file is the open
  question - UIVisualizer registration may well be collected across all matching
  entries rather than winner-takes-all. If it is collected, nothing here is
  needed.

  HOW TO TELL WHICH IT IS

  std::vector<double> and std::vector<gp_XYZ> have NO entry in FCCore.natvis, so
  nothing competes for them. If "Plot with PlotBridge" shows up on a
  vector<double> but not on a vector<gp_Pnt>, precedence is the cause and these
  blocks fix it. If it shows up on neither, the problem is elsewhere and adding
  these will not help.

  WHY SEPARATE <Type> BLOCKS RATHER THAN EDITING THE EXISTING ONE

  natvis.xsd defines the body of <Type> as an xs:choice: either the
  visualization elements (DisplayString, Expand, Intrinsic, ...) or one or more
  <UIVisualizer> elements - never both. So a UIVisualizer cannot be added to the
  existing entry; it has to be its own block. Leave the existing entry, with its
  [chart2d] / [chart3d] synthetics, exactly as it is.

  The ServiceId must match PlotBridgeGuids.Service in the extension.
-->

<UIVisualizer ServiceId="{3f7a1c58-9e2b-4d16-8a54-c6b0f39d7e42}" Id="1"
              MenuName="Plot with PlotBridge" />

<Type Name="std::vector&lt;gp_Pnt,*&gt;">
  <UIVisualizer ServiceId="{3f7a1c58-9e2b-4d16-8a54-c6b0f39d7e42}" Id="1" />
</Type>

<Type Name="std::vector&lt;gp_Pnt2d,*&gt;">
  <UIVisualizer ServiceId="{3f7a1c58-9e2b-4d16-8a54-c6b0f39d7e42}" Id="1" />
</Type>

<Type Name="std::vector&lt;gp_Vec,*&gt;">
  <UIVisualizer ServiceId="{3f7a1c58-9e2b-4d16-8a54-c6b0f39d7e42}" Id="1" />
</Type>

<Type Name="std::vector&lt;gp_Vec2d,*&gt;">
  <UIVisualizer ServiceId="{3f7a1c58-9e2b-4d16-8a54-c6b0f39d7e42}" Id="1" />
</Type>

<Type Name="std::vector&lt;gp_Dir,*&gt;">
  <UIVisualizer ServiceId="{3f7a1c58-9e2b-4d16-8a54-c6b0f39d7e42}" Id="1" />
</Type>

<Type Name="std::vector&lt;gp_Dir2d,*&gt;">
  <UIVisualizer ServiceId="{3f7a1c58-9e2b-4d16-8a54-c6b0f39d7e42}" Id="1" />
</Type>
